WEBVTT

00:00:00.650 --> 00:00:02.037
Give an agent a task.

00:00:02.237 --> 00:00:04.174
Keep control of what happens next.

00:00:04.374 --> 00:00:05.737
Meet Relay OS.

00:00:07.587 --> 00:00:09.499
Type a request into the playground.

00:00:09.699 --> 00:00:15.600
A real language model runs in your browser, choosing tools and working with the available records.

00:00:15.800 --> 00:00:17.550
No API key required.

00:00:19.400 --> 00:00:21.418
Ask for a forty-nine dollar refund.

00:00:21.618 --> 00:00:24.590
The agent looks up the order and retrieves the policy.

00:00:24.790 --> 00:00:29.413
The runtime checks permission, updates the local record, and saves a receipt.

00:00:31.263 --> 00:00:35.294
A two-hundred-and-forty-nine dollar refund needs human approval.

00:00:35.494 --> 00:00:38.109
The action pauses before anything changes.

00:00:38.309 --> 00:00:40.910
Approve it, and the runtime commits the result.

00:00:42.760 --> 00:00:46.006
The refund policy sets a five-hundred dollar ceiling.

00:00:46.206 --> 00:00:48.134
These limits are enforced in code.

00:00:48.334 --> 00:00:50.507
The model cannot grant itself permission.

00:00:52.357 --> 00:00:56.156
Inspect tool inputs, policy decisions, and committed receipts.

00:00:56.356 --> 00:00:58.928
Records and approvals survive a refresh.

00:00:59.128 --> 00:01:01.680
Export the session to see exactly what happened.

00:01:03.530 --> 00:01:04.953
Real model inference.

00:01:05.153 --> 00:01:08.743
Actual local transactions, using fictional business data.

00:01:08.943 --> 00:01:11.925
Explore Relay OS, and put the agent to work.
